{"title":"Mock AIME 1 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> has an inradius of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and a circumradius of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/8/0b853e7b623b0364646078b4bff2d387df4a7739.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cos{B} = \\cos{A} + \\cos{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"183\" height=\"14\" />, then the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/c/11c5ea5774a663fa2517dce85e6d24f66d60f0c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a\\sqrt{b}}{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"35\" height=\"41\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/7/9f73d811eca6419d9c9a27423331d71ff06eb957.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is not divisible by the square of any prime. Compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6ebd1e0356cfe09c0d9b5459d6f1542657bb5891.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/a/04a92037b458c46e4b39d09775b9155c92eb13e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos A + \\cos B + \\cos C = 1+\\frac{r}{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"240\" height=\"33\" />, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/1/d51e8107c616dd2f89a67ef9a7618f33029c99b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos A + \\cos B + \\cos C = \\frac{21}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"214\" height=\"37\" />. From here, combining this with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/7/887d0c3bd8fd0f25eec185eb96e911a05a2857e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cos B = \\cos A + \\cos C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"183\" height=\"14\" />, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/b/b1ba9d7a84167c3a0677813a54473ed0b47b375c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos B = \\frac{7}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"87\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/7/3c71910d0bf49de70af4aee2192c1e2711084f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin B = \\frac{3\\sqrt{23}}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"109\" height=\"41\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/b/edb109c3e4435815b8d0bda65979f07418a09404.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin B = \\frac{b}{2R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"90\" height=\"37\" />, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/7/fd70f04b58f267b6310e27043b94497df1d98d8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 6\\sqrt{23}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" />. By the Law of Cosines, we have that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/b/91b49f37e79e37fc9b12625643f7c77ea242cb53.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b^2 = a^2 + c^2-2ac\\cdot \\cos B \\implies a^2+c^2-\\frac{7ac}{8} = 36 \\cdot 23.\\]\" width=\"431\" height=\"37\" />But one more thing: noting that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/6/87602f4e93b9aa997bcc83cf597e6430ed7f247e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos A = \\frac{b^2+c^2-a^2}{2cb}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"159\" height=\"39\" />. and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/2/5c282f8818000a0bf84972b94a38e1c4a3ba79c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos C = \\frac{a^2+b^2-c^2}{2ab}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"160\" height=\"39\" />, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/b/13b82d954a8a7eb5c1cc689c97ea8b95f1aa09f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{36 \\cdot 23 + b^2+c^2-a^2}{bc} + \\frac{36 \\cdot 23+a^2+b^2-c^2}{ab} = \\frac{7}{4} \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"434\" height=\"39\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/e/9fe25d46f4a326e619c1e4df494d3dd03f2bc5e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{36 \\cdot 23 + c^2-a^2}{c} + \\frac{36 \\cdot 23 + a^2-c^2}{a} = \\frac{21\\sqrt{23}}{2} \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"401\" height=\"41\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/1/a41e6efaefb59e64342a69f846adeb34cacd9b23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(a+c)(36 \\cdot 23 + 2ac-c^2-a^2)}{ac} = \\frac{21\\sqrt{23}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"329\" height=\"43\" />. Combining this with the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/e/53e8d85de9d3f7f8a6395b31ecf6d94e8f7a166a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+c^2 - \\frac{7ac}{8} = 36 \\cdot 23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"180\" height=\"37\" />, we have that: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/5/df5e28d9844766fc1e0ab347c55dd79da1c66734.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(a+c)(-2ac \\cdot \\frac{7}{16}+2ac)}{ac} = \\frac{21\\sqrt{23}}{2} \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"310\" height=\"41\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/9/d198625724317405f4d859f3e888930d09d885ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+c = \\frac{28 \\sqrt{23}}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"118\" height=\"41\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, our semiperimeter is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/7/967a745af537f0882842589896faa2707c468b62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{23\\sqrt{23}}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"54\" height=\"41\" />. Our area, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/0/3e073e251e0ad8a9bee666cbdb5bb0507dad04e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r \\cdot s$\" width=\"30\" height=\"8\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c464baae3be0c3709a7e98216872bb62a37a494.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{115\\sqrt{23}}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"63\" height=\"41\" />, giving us a final answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/e/dbe8e212289d52f45846f77fd920d659e385e243.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{141}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~AopsUser101\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 Pre 2005\">Mock AIME 1 Pre 2005</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005_Problems\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 Pre 2005 Problems\">Problems</a></b>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?t=14769\">Source</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> 